WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.829
There are many capable
animation tools available today,

2
00:00:02.829 --> 00:00:07.133
ranging from JavaScript libraries like
p5.js to full-blown animation and video

3
00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.825
programs like After Effects.

4
00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:10.400
With all of these options,

5
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.224
how do you know which ones are
best for a particular project?

6
00:00:13.224 --> 00:00:15.538
That’s what this presentation
is going to answer.

7
00:00:15.538 --> 00:00:19.502
I will look at each type of animation
that the company wants to produce and give

8
00:00:19.502 --> 00:00:22.726
a recommendation for each while
explaining the reasoning behind it.

9
00:00:22.726 --> 00:00:26.237
But first, I need to explain functional
and non-functional animation.

10
00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:29.809
Basically, an animation that is
solely decoration is non-functional,

11
00:00:29.809 --> 00:00:33.400
and an animation that is part of an
interactive element is functional.

12
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.347
For example, a promotional video
would be non-functional animation,

13
00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:39.587
but a button changing color when hovered
over would be functional animation.

14
00:00:39.587 --> 00:00:41.000
It’s giving feedback to the user.

15
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.400
Websites are generally built with
JavaScript as the programming language.

16
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.002
JavaScript itself has the ability
to animate web page elements,

17
00:00:48.002 --> 00:00:50.350
but this could be extended
by the use of libraries,

18
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.500
JavaScript files that provide
new functionality to a web page.

19
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.025
An example would be p5.js.

20
00:00:55.025 --> 00:00:59.578
It’s a JavaScript library whose aim is
to add drawing and sketching functions to

21
00:00:59.578 --> 00:01:01.300
JavaScript with simple syntax.

22
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.949
It’s a good tool, but I’d recommend
GreenSock for the company’s website.

23
00:01:04.949 --> 00:01:08.690
GreenSock is a collection of JavaScript
libraries that adds all kinds of tools

24
00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.302
to animate web page elements.

25
00:01:10.302 --> 00:01:13.923
Tweens, playback controls and even
simulated physics are possible with

26
00:01:13.923 --> 00:01:17.331
GreenSock. Given that web pages use a
lot of functional animation and that

27
00:01:17.331 --> 00:01:19.400
GreenSock will tightly
integrate with JavaScript,

28
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.697
it makes sense to use
it to animate a website.

29
00:01:21.697 --> 00:01:25.049
The wide variety of tools available
will make nearly any idea possible,

30
00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:28.152
and the developers won’t have to
learn a new language or program.

31
00:01:28.152 --> 00:01:30.658
I’d recommend GreenSock for banner ads,

32
00:01:30.658 --> 00:01:34.414
HTML greetings and interactive
quizzes as well for the same reasons.

33
00:01:34.414 --> 00:01:36.800
Quizzes are especially
well suited for GreenSock,

34
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.133
as it provides a large
number of possibilities

35
00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:40.756
for adding functional animations

36
00:01:40.756 --> 00:01:45.070
to a quiz. Again, the tight integration
with JavaScript is a very nice feature.

37
00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.393
If 3D graphics are desired, WebGL
would be a good option to pursue,

38
00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:51.584
as it provides the ability to have
3D graphics in a web page natively,

39
00:01:51.584 --> 00:01:54.700
but if you aren’t using 3D graphics,
there isn’t much reason for it.

40
00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.398
For promotional videos, however,
I’d recommend After Effects.

41
00:01:58.398 --> 00:02:02.731
It’s a very robust animation application
capable of executing complex ideas and

42
00:02:02.731 --> 00:02:04.800
effects, and it exports video only.

43
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.123
After Effects can import
many types of assets,

44
00:02:07.123 --> 00:02:09.100
so it can be adapted to many workflows.

45
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.302
It can even use 3D graphics
via Cinema 4D technology.

46
00:02:12.302 --> 00:02:14.200
To use these videos on the web,

47
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.647
simply convert the rendered footage to
a suitable file type such as MP4 and

48
00:02:17.647 --> 00:02:19.881
upload it to YouTube
or embed it with HTML.

49
00:02:19.881 --> 00:02:24.095
So, I’ve briefly introduced several
animation tools and recommended which ones

50
00:02:24.095 --> 00:02:25.571
to use for different projects.

51
00:02:25.571 --> 00:02:27.000
My sources are on the screen.

52
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.712
If you want to watch this video again,

53
00:02:28.712 --> 00:02:30.600
simply click the replay button at the end.

54
00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:31.700
Thank you for watching.
